  "worked_solution": "We start by calculating the derivative of $f$ at the point $(8,6).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =3\\sqrt[3]{x} \\\\ {f}^{\u2032}(x) & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-2/3} \\\\ {f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}} \\\\ {f}^{\u2032}(8) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{8}^{2}}} \\\\ {f}^{\u2032}(8) & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(8,6)$ lies on $y=f(x),$ we know that the corresponding point $(6,8)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nFurthermore, the slopes of the tangents to the two respective points are reciprocals. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{\u2032}(6) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(6))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}(8)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
